orthant 1 language

- # `↯/s.105.2` — `Crypto.Error`
+ # `↯/s.105.2` — `Crypto.Error`

- Raised when Enigmatic cannot decode encrypted data.
+ Se lanza cuando Enigmatic no puede decodificar datos cifrados.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- The cryptographic primitive (cipher, signature, or MAC) rejected the
- input. The constructor takes a `reason: Reason` indicating why the
- operation failed; the rendered message is `could not decode the
- encrypted data because $reason`.
+ La primitiva criptográfica (cifrado, firma o MAC) rechazó la entrada. El constructor toma un
+ `reason: Reason` que indica por qué falló la operación; el mensaje representado es
+ `could not decode the encrypted data because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.105.2.1` — `BadPadding`
+ ### `↯/s.105.2.1` — `BadPadding`

- The padding bytes did not match the cipher's expectations — typically
- because the ciphertext was corrupted or the wrong key was supplied
- (authentication-tag mismatch in AEAD modes).
+ Los bytes de relleno no coincidían con lo que esperaba el cifrado, normalmente porque el texto
+ cifrado estaba dañado o se proporcionó una clave equivocada (discrepancia en la etiqueta de
+ autenticación en los modos AEAD).

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.2.1] could not decode the encrypted data because the ciphertext was corrupted or the key was wrong`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.2.1] could not decode the encrypted data because the ciphertext was corrupted or the key was wrong`

- **Resolution.** Confirm the key and IV match those used at encryption
- time; verify the ciphertext has not been truncated or modified in
- transit.
+ **Solución.** Confirma que la clave y el IV coinciden con los usados al cifrar; verifica que el
+ texto cifrado no se ha truncado ni modificado durante la transmisión.

- ### `↯/s.105.2.2` — `IllegalBlockSize`
+ ### `↯/s.105.2.2` — `IllegalBlockSize`

- The input length was not a multiple of the cipher's block size, or
- otherwise incompatible with the cipher's framing.
+ La longitud de la entrada no era un múltiplo del tamaño de bloque del cifrado, o era incompatible
+ de otro modo con el entramado del cifrado.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.2.2] could not decode the encrypted data because the input length was not valid for the cipher`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.2.2] could not decode the encrypted data because the input length was not valid for the cipher`

- **Resolution.** Verify the ciphertext is complete and was produced by
- the same cipher and mode now being used to decrypt it.
+ **Solución.** Verifica que el texto cifrado está completo y que lo produjo el mismo cifrado y modo
+ que se usa ahora para descifrarlo.

- ### `↯/s.105.2.3` — `InvalidKey`
+ ### `↯/s.105.2.3` — `InvalidKey`

- The key bytes were rejected by the cipher — wrong size, invalid
- format, or unsupported parameters.
+ El cifrado rechazó los bytes de la clave: tamaño equivocado, formato no válido o parámetros no
+ admitidos.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.2.3] could not decode the encrypted data because the key was not valid for the cipher`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.2.3] could not decode the encrypted data because the key was not valid for the cipher`

- **Resolution.** Confirm the key was produced for the same cipher and
- parameter set.
+ **Solución.** Confirma que la clave se produjo para el mismo cifrado y conjunto de parámetros.

- ### `↯/s.105.2.4` — `InvalidAlgorithm`
+ ### `↯/s.105.2.4` — `InvalidAlgorithm`

- The requested algorithm or mode is not available in the JVM's
- configured providers.
+ El algoritmo o modo solicitado no está disponible en los proveedores configurados de la JVM.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.2.4] could not decode the encrypted data because the algorithm was not available`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.2.4] could not decode the encrypted data because the algorithm was not available`

- **Resolution.** Install or enable a JCA provider that supports the
- algorithm; check `java.security` policy.
+ **Solución.** Instala o habilita un proveedor JCA que admita el algoritmo; comprueba la política
+ de `java.security`.

- ### `↯/s.105.2.5` — `IoFailure`
+ ### `↯/s.105.2.5` — `IoFailure`

- The cipher implementation could not read or write the data buffers —
- typically a low-level I/O fault.
+ La implementación del cifrado no pudo leer ni escribir los búferes de datos, normalmente por un
+ fallo de E/S de bajo nivel.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.2.5] could not decode the encrypted data because data could not be read or written`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.2.5] could not decode the encrypted data because data could not be read or written`

- **Resolution.** Inspect the cause chain for the underlying I/O error.
+ **Solución.** Examina la cadena de causas en busca del error de E/S subyacente.

